# Pages & Routing

## File naming

- Pages: `*.page.tsx` (e.g. `login.page.tsx`, `user-list.page.tsx`)
- Folder barrels: `index.ts` re-exports; root surface is `src/pages/index.ts`

## Pattern

Pages stay thin: layout + feature form/module. Export a `Secure*` wrapper when auth/flags/permissions apply.

```tsx
function LoginPage() {
  const { t } = useTranslation();
  return (
    <AuthFormLayout title={t('auth:login.title')} subtitle={t('auth:login.subtitle')}>
      <LoginForm />
    </AuthFormLayout>
  );
}

export const SecureLoginPage = SecurityGuard(LoginPage, {
  redirect: PageURLS.home,
  requiresNoAuth: true,
  featureFlags: [FEATURE_FLAG.areAuthPagesEnabled, FEATURE_FLAG.isLoginPageEnabled],
});
```

Admin example: `requiresAuth: true`, `andPermissions: [PERMISSION.*]`, `redirect: PageURLS.auth.login`.

## Checklist for a new page

1. Add `*.page.tsx` under the right folder (`auth/`, `admin/`, or root `pages/`)
2. Re-export from folder `index.ts` and `src/pages/index.ts` if needed
3. Register route in `src/core/router.tsx` under the matching layout (`RouterAuthLayout` / `RouterPageLayout`)
4. Add URL helper on `PageURLS` in `src/core/constants.ts`
5. Wire `SecurityGuard` + `FEATURE_FLAG` / `PERMISSION` as peers do

Prefer `PageURLS.*` and `viewTransition` on links over hard-coded paths.
